.lake
*~
__pycache__/
# Parser table cache that BitBake writes into the current directory whenever
# it cannot write to its own install location (e.g. the read-only
# /opt/bitbake in the sandbox container).
pyshtables.py
# Default top directory of bitbake-setup when it is run from the repo root
# without the top-dir settings (see doc/building/building_imx93_images.md).
# It holds build directories with per-user settings such as
# conf/toolcfg.conf, which records the person's own acceptance of the NXP
# EULA, and must never be committed.
/bitbake-builds/
